.TH RAYGUI 2
.SH NAME
raygui \- immediate-mode controls for raylib
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <u.h>
.br
.B #include <libc.h>
.br
.B #include <raylib.h>
.br
.B #include <raygui.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Raygui provides buttons, text boxes, check boxes, sliders, lists, dialogs,
color pickers, styles and embedded icons on top of
.IR raylib (2).
The caller owns the control state and layout.
Controls read raylib's input and draw inside the caller's existing frame;
there is no additional window or event loop.
.PP
Compile with
.BR -p .
The header selects
.B libraygui.a
at link time. Do not define
.B RAYGUI_IMPLEMENTATION
in a client; the implementation is already compiled into the library.
The header documents the individual controls and their return values.
.PP
The style and active control state are global to the process.
Call controls between
.B BeginDrawing
and
.BR EndDrawing .
Editable text buffers belong to the caller; pass their capacity in bytes,
including space for the terminating NUL.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
void
main(void)
{
    bool grid = true;

    InitWindow(400, 200, "controls");
    SetTargetFPS(60);
    while(!WindowShouldClose()){
        BeginDrawing();
        ClearBackground(RAYWHITE);
        GuiCheckBox((Rectangle){20,20,20,20}, "Grid", &grid);
        if(GuiButton((Rectangle){20,60,100,30}, "Reset"))
            grid = true;
        EndDrawing();
    }
    CloseWindow();
    exits(nil);
}
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libraygui
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR modelview (1),
.IR raylib (2),
.IR tinygl (2)
.SH BUGS
Controls require explicit layout and clipping by the application.
The library is not thread-safe and inherits raylib's platform limits.
